  "question": {
    "text": "Based on Heisenberg's uncertainty principle, the uncertainty in the velocity of the electron to be found within an atomic nucleus of diameter \\(10^{-15} \\mathrm{~m}\\) is ________. \\(10^9 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\\) (nearest integer)\n[Given : mass of electron \\(=9.1 \\times 10^{-31} \\mathrm{~kg}\\), Plank's constant \\((h)=6.626 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{Js}\\)] (Value of \\(\\pi=3.14\\))",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "58",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{m} \\Delta \\mathrm{V} . \\Delta \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{4 \\pi} \\\\ & \\begin{aligned} \\Delta \\mathrm{V} & =\\frac{6.626 \\times 10^{-34}}{9.1 \\times 10^{-31} \\times 10^{-15} \\times 4 \\times 3.14} \\\\ & =57.97 \\times 10^{+9} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
